<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Agathocles (son of Lysimachus)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 283 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Agathocles was the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lysimachus">Lysimachus</a>, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a>, and a successful commander for his father. Around 283 BCE Lysimachus had him executed on a charge of treason, reportedly at the instigation of his stepmother Arsinoe II. The killing caused defections to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucus-i-nicator">Seleucus I</a>, who defeated and killed Lysimachus at Corupedium in 281 BCE.</p></div>
